# Sidelit application · Operate / Read

## Direction contract

THESIS: Keep a developer in the render–inspect–instruct loop without losing their reading position. Rex is the explicitly requested visual reference; preserve Sidelit's navigation and editing model.

OWN-WORLD: Blue-charcoal pane and chrome layers, quiet SF-style labels and outline icons, violet for intentional actions, softly rounded tabs and an inset work pane. Light mode is the same hierarchy on cool pale surfaces.

STORY: Open a supported document, read and select a passage or inspect an element, send an Explain, Review, or Edit request to Pi, then stay at the same passage when disk changes arrive. Answers appear in Pi, with Show in Rex for a linked session.

FIRST VIEWPORT: A 48px compact toolbar above a 240px resizable explorer and an inset preview pane. Rounded file tabs lead the pane. Rendered Markdown begins in reading mode with explicit Edit. Text selection exposes adjacent Explain/Review/Edit actions. The compact composer anchors near the selection when space allows and docks at the lower right in narrow windows or without a usable anchor. At 1000px and below toolbar action labels become accessible icons.

FORM: User-pinned native Rex reference, code-led. No invented alternative direction or approval round. Scroll anchoring is the signature behavior, not a decorative effect.

FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance

## Selection workflow

- **Read and edit:** toolbar Edit enables direct Markdown editing; Done editing, tab changes, and mode changes return it to reading. Request Edit is a separate Pi intent. Explain and Review ask for answers without file changes; their instruction is optional, while Edit needs an instruction.
- **Keep one request:** Hide or Escape dismisses the composer without discarding it. Request reopens the same draft or delivery state across tabs. Selecting different content offers Use new selection before the first send, preserving the instruction and intent when accepted. Discard request and the post-receipt New request clear it explicitly. One quick request remains in memory. Add to review explicitly saves notes locally; Notes opens a compact list for editing, removal, reveal, selection, payload review, and one-message batch delivery. Saved notes and one immutable delivery attempt survive restart. This adds no chat history or task tracking.
- **Keep the capture honest:** the request retains its path/URL, capture time, bounded excerpt, and available file revision/disk hash. Attached context shows the excerpt, location, capture time, and available element details; inferred source lines and shortened excerpts are labelled. Unsaved captures warn that Pi can read the disk version; changed or closed file context is stale and requires Send the captured version before the first send. Live pages carry a separate uncertainty notice. Sending does not save the document or refresh its attachment.
- **Reconnect to the passage:** the retained attachment can stay highlighted when native selection or composer focus changes. Reveal selection returns to its document and hides the composer. Reattachment requires a unique text anchor or a matching element; page URL mismatches also fail closed. An unresolved capture reports that it cannot be located, and a closed document must be reopened first. Preview inspection keeps its existing sandbox and development-server bridge opt-in.
- **Deliver deliberately:** show the Pi target explicitly and require a choice when no remembered connected target or sole connected session resolves it. The first attempt locks intent, instruction, target, and context; retries retain the same message ID and payload. Received, queued, and accepted are delivery states, with answers in Pi and Show in Rex only for a linked Rex block.
- **Keep delivery visible:** the existing chrome, line border, radii, and compact action styling frame a single-column composer. Intent/Hide stays above the scrolling context and instruction body; target, Send/Retry, discard/new-request action, and status stay below it outside the scroller. Selection anchoring applies at 1000px and wider when space permits; smaller windows use the bounded lower-right dock.

## Evidence and finish status

This is an ordinary extension of the existing visual system. Documentation was reconciled against `src/App.tsx`, `src/Rich.tsx`, `src/FeedbackComposer.tsx`, `src/SelectionActions.tsx`, and `src/style.css`, with `src/inspection.ts`, `src/selection-dom.ts`, `src/agent-targets.ts`, `src/Preview.tsx`, and `extensions/preview-bridge/sidelit.js` checked for capture, target, and reattachment behavior. Existing token values and the layout world are retained. This pass used source inspection only; it ran no app, browser, tests, or servers and makes no new measurement or visual-verdict claim. Final capture review and the visual verdict belong to the separate reviewer. No comps or raster assets were generated.

